{
  "_comment": {
    "Crimson Slate node editor palette, Ironforge revision. Keys and": 0,
    "structure mirror themes/Dark/nodes_theme.json exactly; only values": 0,
    "differ. Same tokens as the header of theme.qss -- keep them in step,": 0,
    "or the node editor is the one window that stayed blue-grey.": 0,
    "$bg.void     = #100E0B;  16, 14, 11": 0,
    "$bg.alt      = #1D1916;  29, 25, 22": 0,
    "$bg.panel    = #292621;  41, 38, 33": 0,
    "$bg.raised   = #3C3732;  60, 55, 50": 0,
    "$stroke.soft = #403B35;  64, 59, 53": 0,
    "$stroke      = #565049;  86, 80, 73": 0,
    "$accent      = #E5405C; 229, 64, 92": 0,
    "$accent.hi   = #F3687F; 243, 104, 127": 0,
    "THE ACCENT IS CRIMSON. It was gold; the whole application moved with": 0,
    "it, and the status ramp moved too so that 'selected' and 'this is": 0,
    "broken' are not the same red -- see the ACCENT and STATUS sections at": 0,
    "the head of theme.qss for the arithmetic.": 0,
    "The node body is FLAT: all four gradient stops are bg.raised, because": 0,
    "the rest of the theme has no gradient in it and a shaded node would be": 0,
    "the one place the old look survived.": 0,
    "WHICH CRIMSON GOES WHERE follows the same surface rule the sheet": 0,
    "states: plain accent only where both neighbours are bg.void, bg.alt or": 0,
    "bg.panel, otherwise accent.hi. A selected node BOUNDARY and a filled": 0,
    "connection point both sit against the bg.raised node body, where accent": 0,
    "measures 2.925:1 and misses the 3:1 floor, so both take accent.hi at": 0,
    "3.977:1 on the body and 6.513:1 on the bg.void canvas. A selected": 0,
    "CONNECTION is drawn on the canvas, where plain accent is 4.790:1, and": 0,
    "its halo takes accent.hi at 6.513:1 so the two are 1.360:1 apart.": 0,
    "Connections at rest use the reserved categorical green (ok), never the": 0,
    "accent, so a selected connection and a normal one are never the same": 0,
    "hue -- 157.0 degrees apart, and 124.8 between ok and error.": 0,
    "Error is bad #EF752E and warning is warn #D8AB18. Against the crimson": 0,
    "accent those are 32.3 and 56.1 degrees. Under the OLD crimson accent": 0,
    "error was 4.0 degrees away and effectively the same colour; that is the": 0,
    "collision this revision fixes by moving the ERROR rather than the": 0,
    "accent. On the bg.void canvas bad is 6.657:1 and warn 8.955:1, and on": 0,
    "the bg.raised node body 4.065:1 and 5.468:1.": 0
  },
